      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6"><h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Life Sciences</h3><p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">Drug discovery, clinical trial optimization, genomic analysis, research mining, and regulatory compliance for pharma and biotech.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 13. FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS -->
<section class="py-20 md:py-28" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="faq-heading"
      index="13"
      label="Frequently Asked Questions"
      title="Common questions about AI-native engineering."
      lede="Enterprise leaders evaluating AI-native engineering have specific concerns about strategy, architecture, security, and implementation."
    />
    <div class="mt-14 max-w-4xl space-y-4" data-reveal-group>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>What is the difference between AI-native and AI-enabled applications?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">AI-enabled apps add AI features to existing architectures. AI-native apps are architected from the ground up with AI as a first-class concern. The distinction determines whether AI becomes a competitive advantage or a costly add-on.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How long does it take to build a production AI system?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">A focused prototype can be delivered in 4-6 weeks. A production pilot takes 8-16 weeks. Full enterprise AI platforms may take 3-6 months. We structure engagements to deliver value incrementally at each phase.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do I choose between LLMs and SLMs?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">LLMs excel at complex reasoning and broad knowledge. SLMs are better for focused tasks requiring low latency and cost efficiency. Many systems use both: an SLM for routing, an LLM for reasoning, and embedding models for retrieval.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>What is RAG and when should I use it?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">RAG connects models to your knowledge base by retrieving relevant information before generating a response. It is recommended when your system needs to answer based on specific business data, maintain accuracy with evolving information, or reduce hallucination risk.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>When should I fine-tune versus use RAG?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Fine-tuning is appropriate when the model needs to adopt a specific style or internalize specialized knowledge. RAG is better when knowledge changes often. Many production systems use both.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do AI agents differ from traditional automation?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Traditional automation follows predefined rules. AI agents reason about goals, make decisions in ambiguity, and use tools dynamically. Agents suit tasks involving judgment and multiple possible paths.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do you ensure AI system security?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Multi-layer security: prompt injection prevention, data leakage protection, authentication for AI APIs, secrets management, network isolation, content filtering, rate limiting, and audit logging for all AI interactions.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>What is responsible AI and how do you implement it?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Responsible AI encompasses fairness, transparency, accountability, and privacy. We implement bias detection, explainability, privacy-preserving techniques, human oversight, and compliance documentation.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do you handle data privacy and compliance?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Data classification, access controls, encryption at rest and in transit, data anonymization, audit logging, and compliance frameworks aligned with GDPR, HIPAA, SOC 2, and EU AI Act requirements.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>What is the difference between MLOps and LLMOps?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">MLOps focuses on traditional ML pipelines: model training, feature stores, experiment tracking, and deployment. LLMOps extends this with prompt management, response validation, cost tracking per token, and evaluation of generative output quality.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do you optimize AI infrastructure costs?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Through model selection (SLMs vs. LLMs), caching strategies, prompt optimization, request batching, GPU instance right-sizing, spot instance usage, auto-scaling, and cost allocation tracking per team or feature.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>What AI governance frameworks do you recommend?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">We recommend a layered framework: model registry and versioning, approval workflows for model promotion, bias and fairness monitoring, explainability documentation, audit trails, and compliance reporting aligned with regulatory requirements.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>Can you work with our existing cloud infrastructure?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Yes. We design AI systems that integrate with existing AWS, Azure, or GCP infrastructure. Our platform engineering approach extends your current investments rather than replacing them.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>Do you build on open-source or proprietary technologies?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Both, based on your requirements. We are vendor-neutral and recommend the right technology for each use case. We have deep expertise in open-source LLMs, frameworks, and infrastructure, as well as commercial platforms.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do you measure AI system performance in production?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Through multiple dimensions: accuracy (ground truth comparisons), relevance (retrieval quality metrics), latency (p50/p95/p99), cost (per-query token usage), user satisfaction (feedback scores), and safety (guardrail trigger rates).</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>What is your approach to AI vendor lock-in prevention?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">We use abstraction layers that decouple applications from specific model providers, vector databases, and cloud platforms. Standardized interfaces, multi-provider support, and open standards ensure you can switch without rewriting.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do you handle model hallucinations in production?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Through RAG architecture (grounding responses in retrieved knowledge), prompt engineering (explicit instructions to not fabricate), response validation (checking claims against sources), confidence thresholds, and human review for high-stakes outputs.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>What team composition do you recommend for AI-native development?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">We recommend cross-functional teams: AI/ML engineers, software engineers, platform engineers, data engineers, UX designers, and product managers. The specific composition depends on your use case, scale, and maturity.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>How do you handle model updates and versioning?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Through model registry with versioning, automated evaluation against baselines before promotion, canary deployment with traffic shifting, A/B testing in production, automated rollback on performance degradation, and detailed changelogs.</div>
      </details>
      <details class="group rounded-lg border border-line-2 bg-paper open:border-accent transition-colors" data-reveal>
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-between p-5 text-sm font-medium text-ink hover:text-accent transition-colors [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <span>Do you provide managed operations after deployment?</span>
          <svg class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 2v12M2 8h12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-5 pb-5 text-sm text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">Yes. We offer managed AI operations including monitoring, incident response, cost optimization, model updates, and continuous improvement. SLAs are defined based on your requirements and criticality.</div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

